## REPORT BACK — batch E (PRES-C), increment 001

**Verdict implemented:** PRES-C (one interactive surface), SVG+PNG export, `R` replaces the report. The prototype `build.py`/`variants.py` were re-derived into `taskboard/views.py` (no pasted port), and `R`'s seat is now the presentation.

### What changed (file:line)

- `taskboard/views.py:5867` `present_project_id` — selected task's project, else focused, else first visible project.
- `taskboard/views.py:5881` `present_tasks` — (open by due, all) of one project in gantt order.
- `taskboard/views.py:6032` `render_present` — the PRES-C frame: gantt field on top (today rule `bright`, accent = cursor only), brief one-liners below, `⟦━⟧` cursor whose task's notes expand. S1 throughout.
- `taskboard/views.py:6082` `present_paths` — `reports/present-<slug>-<date>.svg/.png` (the shipped report destination).
- `taskboard/views.py:6093` `save_present_svg` — rich `save_svg`, writing to devnull so width-1 glyphs never hit the Windows cp1252 encoder.
- `taskboard/views.py:6106` `_find_msedge` — Edge from standard install locations, then `shutil.which`.
- `taskboard/views.py:6118` `save_present_png` — rasterizes the SVG with headless Edge (`--screenshot … --window-size=<W*10>,<H*20> file:///<svg>`), short timeout, exit-code captured; `None` when absent/failed.
- `taskboard/app.py:182` `PresentScreen`; `taskboard/app.py:240` `_paint`; `taskboard/app.py:258` `action_export` (SVG always; PNG needs-Edge toast on `None`); `taskboard/app.py:704` `action_present` (replaces `action_report`).
- `taskboard/keymap.py:136` `R` → `present`/`Present`.
- `README.md` — `R` row → Present/Standup; new "Presentation" section; `reports/` note.

Two fixes on top of the pre-existing work in this tree: (1) `save_present_png` was PIL-based — rewritten to headless Edge per LLR-1001.2; (2) `PresentScreen._render` shadowed Textual's `Widget._render` (crashed the screen) — renamed to `_paint`.

### Oracle diff result

Rendered through the real `render_present` on the kg fixture (`pweb`, cursor `tw3`, TODAY 2026-09-30): **all rows byte-identical** at both `PRES-C-118x30.txt` and `PRES-C-80x24.txt` (30/30 and 24/24 rows match). The export smoke test also wrote a real SVG (22 KB) and Edge-rasterized PNG (72 KB) to `reports/`.

### Suite counts

`env -u NO_COLOR TERM=xterm-256color COLORTERM=truecolor PYTHONIOENCODING=utf-8 python -m pytest tests -q` → **2524 passed, 5 failed**. All 5 are test-side REDs from `R` moving report→present (the brief's "tests agent owns the test side"); no source bug behind them.

### Census RED named

1. `tests/test_keymap.py::test_the_palette_includes_palette_only_globals` — `GLOBAL_ACTIONS` still lists `report`; the seat's `R` action is now `present`.
2. `tests/test_markup_census.py::test_TC_401_no_textual_sink_takes_a_markup_str` — new site `app.py PresentScreen._paint update(text <- render_present(...))` needs the D-405 EXEMPT entry (like `refresh_view`/`_repaint_flow`).
3. `tests/test_markup_sites.py::test_AT_403_typed_and_os_text_is_painted_exactly` — the `R` arm expects `Report written to …`; `R` now opens the presentation.
4. `tests/test_report.py::test_the_report_key_is_in_the_seat` — looks up `action == "report"`.
5. `tests/test_report.py::test_pressing_R_writes_the_report_and_reports_the_path` — presses `R` expecting the HTML report.
